      },
      {
        "key": "tm9s-pkg5Cc17R1",
        "unstructured": "There has been significant experimental progress in studying optical analogs of quantum backflow, where the instantaneous local momentum of a light field is shown to point opposite to the local momentum of its constituent modes. Such effects have been demonstrated in linear motion using classical optical beams [18, 19] and in rotational motion using both classical light [20] and single photons [21]. However, because these experiments are effectively time independent, they do not capture the probability dynamics that fundamentally define quantum backflow.",
        "type": "other"
      },
